  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nFrontal boundary across southeast Ohio will slowly sag south across \nthe area as surface low continues to push off to our east. Showers \nand storms will continue to occur through this evening, as the front \nslides south, particularly if any breaks in the cloud cover are able \nto form.  Showers and storms will continue to be a possibility on \nFriday, mainly across the far south and east, as a shortwave crosses \nthe area. \n\nFocus then shifts to the weekend, with a deeper upper trough taking \nhold across the area, with a cold front moving through the region. \nSome storms could be strong to severe on Saturday, with a damaging \nwind threat, with decent instability, and drier air in the lower \nlevels/dcape approaching 1000 J/Kg. Drier conditions take hold \nbehind the departing system for Sunday into the first part of next \nweek.",
